-- title:
--   Twisting the full level by χ(h) shifts the label from g to hg
-- statement:
--   The statement is a single implication inside a large frame of hypotheses describing the Čerednik–Drinfeld situation for fake elliptic curves. The frame is listed group by group.
--
--   Arithmetic data. Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), and a level $N \neq 0$ divisible by neither (`hrN`, `hrbarN`) and squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   The base ring. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $\pi$ generating the same ideal as $r$ (`hunr`), together with a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   The unramified cover. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) satisfying `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ precisely when $\det g$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ times $\pi^{n}$.
--
--   The indefinite quaternion side. Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar` ($0<a$ or $0<b$, and the completion at a finite place is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$), and $\Lambda$ a maximal order (`hΛ`: an order maximal among orders).
--
--   Coarse and fine moduli. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point map $\mathrm{pt}$ assigning to every fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$ a point of $\mathcal X$ over the given base morphism, and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullbacks, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`) and coprime to $N$ (`hnN`); a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map $\mathrm{ptF}$ on curves with full level-$n$ structure and `hM : IsFineModuli` (isomorphism invariance, pullback compatibility, surjectivity and injectivity of the point map on all rings). A group $G$ with $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and a label map $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (each $\rho(g)$ lies over the base; twisting a full level by $\chi(g)$ composes the point with $\rho(g)$; $\chi(1) \equiv 1$ and $\chi(gg') \equiv \chi(g)\chi(g')$ modulo $n\Lambda$; and $\chi$ is a bijection onto the invertible classes modulo $n$). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`), compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`).
--
--   Hecke and Atkin–Lehner structure. For every prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base with point map $\mathrm{ptT}$ on curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure and `h𝒴 : IsCoarseModuliT`, and degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) computing, on points, the underlying curve (`hd₀`) and the quotient by the level-$\ell$ subgroup (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   The definite quaternion side. Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$ (`hdef`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); the place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$ (`hv`). The group $\Gamma_t$ is characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at every place other than $v$. Elements $s(\ell) \in \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and ideles $s_f(\ell)$ for $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ subject to `hs`: $s_f(\ell)$ is the diagonal image of $s(\ell)$ at each place not above $r$ and is $1$ at the places above $r$; the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $s_f(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of the pair $(\Lambda_1, R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}\,s(\ell) = \ell$. The groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ are the intersections of $\Gamma_t$ with its conjugate by $s(\ell)$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   The reduction at $r$. All integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r}^{(2)} \times \mathbb Z_{r}^{(2)}$ satisfies `IsOrderCoord` (additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product, injective, with dense image, and compatible with reduced traces). Over the residue ring $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ for $A_0$ with `hA₀ : A₀.IsFormalModuleVia coord X₀ θ₀`, and families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e(\gamma)$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg \gamma$. The hypotheses on these (summarised here) are: `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $e$ up to multiplications by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act through integer multiplications), `hE1'` (converse: if $e\gamma$ becomes an integer multiplication up to a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\, g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (the action of $\Gamma_t$ on any full level-$n$ structure of $A_0$ is given by labels $\mathrm{lab}\,\gamma \in \Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$), `hE4` (every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny of a curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ is accounted for by some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), and `hE5a`–`hE5e` together with `hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r` (an order $R_2 \le R_1$, $r$-adically dense in $R_1$, acts on $A_0$ through $\hat e$ compatibly with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level, multiplicatively, through integer multiplications on integers, with $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ the multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}\,x$, matching $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$, and realised simultaneously with $e$ in $M_2(K_0)$ by one conjugator $g$).
--
--   The Drinfeld side. A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r}^{(2)} \to \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a comparison map $\eta$ from rigidified objects attached to $\Phi$ to $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible rigidified objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies exactly the isomorphic ones; $\eta$ is natural in the base; every point of $MD$ is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$); and an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable to $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the two-sided sense of `hE₀`. The Drinfeld dictionary consists of $e_D$ together with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity over every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent), `hfstD` (the first leg of $e_D$ is the structure map), `hGLD` ($e_D$ intertwines the action of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ on points of $\mathcal G(\mathcal O, MD)$ with the twisted action on pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-point and a Deligne datum), `hPiD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to a single Frobenius twist of the first leg), and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates). Further, $\kappa$ with `hκ` relating the quotient by $\pi$ to the quotient by $r$, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to the $\kappa$-pushforward of $X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   The Atkin–Lehner witness at $\bar r$ in the reduction. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; a curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`) such that $(a_w,a_w')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving the level (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` (one conjugator $g$ realises simultaneously all $e\gamma$ as in `hE2` and the composite $a_w \text{ followed by } b_w$ as $r^{k_w}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$).
--
--   The dictionary $\Xi$. A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to a point of $\mathcal G(\mathcal O, MD)$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the first leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of the given $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullbacks of rigidifications), `hΞiso` ($\Xi$ is constant on rigidified curves related by an isomorphism of curves together with a comparison of the rigidification data up to $r$-power multiplications), and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, if the curve carries a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ via $\mathrm{coord}$ then there are $j \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, transporting $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, such that $\Xi$ equals the point built from $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and $\eta(t)$). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ moves $\Xi$ by the action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$) and `heqW` (over connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible, an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ together with the indicated comparison of rigidifications moves $\Xi$ by the action of $r^{c} g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   The representing object for rigidified full-level data. A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ with $\pi$ nilpotent (`hCπ`) and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi_C : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to C$; a functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras and a point map $\mathrm{ptR}$ assigning to a $C$-algebra $S$ whose $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg is $\chi_C$, a curve with full level-$n$ structure and a rigidification of it relative to $A_0$, an element of $PR(S)$; subject to `hR2` (naturality in $S$ for pullbacks of the curve, the level point and the rigidification), `hR3s` (every element of $PR(S)$ is such a point), `hR3i` (over $S$ with no idempotents besides $0,1$, equality of two points yields an isomorphism of the curves respecting group law, $\Lambda$-action, level subscheme and level-$n$ point, together with a comparison of the rigidifications up to $r$-power multiplications), and `hR1` (conversely, such an isomorphism and comparison force equality of the two points).
--
--   The data of the assertion. A nontrivial Noetherian ring $S$ which is a $C$-algebra and an $\mathcal O$-algebra compatibly, in which the only idempotents are $0$ and $1$ (`hc`) and in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hS`); the leg $\psi_S : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by the structure map (`hψS`); a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u_1$ relative to $\psi_S$; elements $h, g \in G$, an index $j \in \{0,1\}$, and a full level-$n$ structure $P'$ on the same curve $u_1$ with $P'.P = \chi(h) \cdot u_2.P$, that is, the image of the level point of $u$ under the action of $\chi(h)$ (`hP'`).
--
--   Conclusion. Assume that the point $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$, namely that there exist a witness that $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_1 : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by the structure map, a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u_1$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho_1$ of $u_{1,1}$ relative to $\psi_1$ such that: (i) $\mathrm{ptR}(u_1,\rho_1) = \mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho)$; (ii) there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_{n,1}$ on $u_{1,1}$ which is a normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\rho_1$ in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport Fr θ₀ κ β₀ Φ ι coord P₀` (a section $Q$ of the reduced auxiliary curve lying over the reduction of $P_0$, a formal module structure on $u_{1,1}$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, an exponent $j' \le 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ transporting $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$, such that the reduction of the $r^{t.n}$-multiple of $P_{n,1}$ is the image of $Q$), and the level point of $u_1$ equals $\chi(g) \cdot P_{n,1}$; (iii) the first leg of $\Xi(u_{1,1},\rho_1)$ is $\psi_1 \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$.
--
--   Then the point $\mathrm{ptR}(\langle u_1, P'\rangle, \rho)$ admits a presentation of label $(hg, j)$: there exist a witness that $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi_2 : \mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by the structure map, a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u_2$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho_2$ of $u_{2,1}$ relative to $\psi_2$, such that $\mathrm{ptR}(u_2,\rho_2) = \mathrm{ptR}(\langle u_1, P'\rangle, \rho)$; there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_{n,2}$ on $u_{2,1}$ which is a normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\rho_2$ in the same sense, with the level point of $u_2$ equal to $\chi(hg) \cdot P_{n,2}$; and the first leg of $\Xi(u_{2,1},\rho_2)$ is $\psi_2 \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$.
--
--   A bookkeeping step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the moduli of fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure: the label in $G$ attached to a point of the rigidified full-level functor is shifted by left multiplication when the level structure is twisted by $\chi(h)$, while the Frobenius-twist index $j$ is unchanged, in accordance with the diagrammatic composition $\mathrm{act}(xy) = \mathrm{act}\,y$ followed by $\mathrm{act}\,x$. It feeds the naturality statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_label_natural_iff_exists_ptR_eq_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr), and uses only the existence of a $\chi(h)$-twist of a given full level structure on a fixed curve.
